    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c1_parity_r0_jacobi_norm_transfer",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=1 parity R0 has a shared two-sign Jacobi-norm interface",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For R0, put a=(r+r^-1)/2, x=2a^2-1, and epsilon=r^(2^40). The primary gap, source torsion, and lift-free constant gate are exactly C_(2M)^(1/4)(x)=0, the epsilon Chebyshev factor, and (1+epsilon P_(4M-1)(x)^2)^2+x^2-1=0. The even-Jacobi transform gives one degree-2^36 gcd per sign with F_epsilon=(1+epsilon zQ^2)^2+z-1. Its torsion-only resultants are exactly the existing CR-002 order-2^39 norm and 37-level plus tower, so no separate large R0 norm run is needed. The norms and signed gcds remain unevaluated.",
